From 932e266beef6424c9f1962a0f112cd7495ab15c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PathOps <noreply@pathops.dev>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:41:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] auth: PathOps repository tokens and deploy keys for
 BUILD_AND_PUSH

PathOps Decision 0056 provisions an Application's BUILD_AND_PUSH access
as the user, with delegated tokens, in two read-only credentials of the
source repository:

- pathops_repository_token (owner, repository, name, scopes
  ["read:repository"], actions create|revoke): list the user's access
  tokens, create exactly that named token readable only for that one
  repository (the Tekton resolver's), and delete it by that exact name
  (an orphan left when the creation's answer was lost). The name can
  never be taken for a token id.
- pathops_deploy_key (owner, repository, title, read_only true, actions
  configure): list the repository's deploy keys and add one with that
  title, read_only present and true (it defaults to false).
- pathops_repository gains the read action: the repository and its git
  trees, without the create/seed write authority.

Access token creation and deletion are basic-auth-only routes;
ReqBasicOrRevProxyAuth lets a PathOps delegated token through them,
since its authorization_details authorized the exact request before
routing. Every other token is still refused there.
